    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1393">

                <pb facs="1740" n="1540" xml:id="pg1540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Mikołajczyk Papers</note>
                <head>No. 1393<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Diary Entry by the Polish Deputy Prime
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mikołajczyk</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1393-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-31">July 31, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Harriman called in the afternoon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1393-f2"/> On behalf
                    of President Truman, as chairman of the meeting of the Big Three which began at
                    4 o’clock, he invited the Polish Delegation to see President Truman the next
                    day, when the latter would communicate the results of the meeting today.…</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1393-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1393-f1-content">
                <p>Cf. <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg541">p. 541</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1393-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1393-f2-content">
                <p>From the discussion which took place toward the end of the Eleventh Plenary
                    Meeting on July 31, it would appear that Harriman probably paid his call on the
                    Polish Delegation following the adjournment of that meeting at 7:15 p.m. Cf. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg527">pp. 527</ref>–<ref
                        target="#pg528">528</ref>, <ref target="#pg538">538</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
